      "type": "output",
      "content": "# Reduce game asset payload and preload cost â€” result\n\n## What shipped (verified, no tooling required)\nFixed `preloadTileImages()` in `game.js` so startup preloads only the small hex-cropped board tiles (`img/tiles/<base>_hex.png`) instead of the full-resolution tile art (`img/tiles/<base>.png`).\n\nThe board renders `getTileImg(t, \"hex\")` â†’ `_hex.png` in `render()`. The full-res art is used **only** by on-demand views â€” `setTileHeroSprite()`, `tileImgHtml()`, and the tooltip hero â€” which already fetch lazily when their element is displayed. So eager full-res preloading warmed ~150 MB the board never uses. The new version also dedupes shared files (e.g. `signal-tower.png`).\n\n## Measured before/after (31 mapped tiles)\n| Metric | Before (full-res preload) | After (hex preload) | Reduction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Preload network payload | **150.4 MB** | **20.8 MB** | **âˆ’129.6 MB (âˆ’86%)** |\n| Decoded RGBA memory | **412.5 MB** | **21.3 MB** | **âˆ’391.2 MB (âˆ’95%)** |\n\n(Sample dimensions: `crash-site.png` 2760Ã—1504 full-res vs `crash-site_hex.png` 400Ã—450.)\nDecoded memory is the larger runtime win â€” the browser no longer decodes ~410 MB of RGBA for images that are never shown on the board. Full-res art still loads on demand when a player opens a tile detail/hero/tooltip, so nothing is visually lost.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --check game.js` â†’ OK\n- `node --test test/game-logic.test.js` â†’ **31 passed, 0 failed**\n- Confirmed all 31 mapped tiles have a `_hex.png` variant (0 missing â†’ no 404 risk)\n- Confirmed no other code path relies on eager full-res preloading (all full-res consumers fetch on demand)\n\n## Deferred â€” blocked on absent tooling (honest, not done)\nThe task also asked to \"convert oversized web audio/images to compressed formats.\" This environment has **no** media tooling:\n- `ffmpeg`, `cwebp`, `magick`/ImageMagick: **all missing from PATH**\n- **No `node_modules` directory at all** â€” `sharp` is not installed (and not even a declared dependency)\n- 0 `.webp` files exist; 52 `.wav` sfx (112 MB) and 390 MB of `img/` remain uncompressed\n\nImage WebP conversion and audio re-encoding therefore **cannot be performed here** and are **not marked complete**. This is the same root cause that killed the 6 prior watchdog re-dispatches (agents attempting conversion/`npm install` with no codecs available). I did not fake progress.\n\n### Recommendation\nSplit re-encoding into a separate task on a tooling-equipped machine:\n1. Install `ffmpeg` + `cwebp` (or ImageMagick), or `npm install sharp` for images.\n2. Convert full-res tile art and sfx to WebP/compressed audio; downscale the grossly oversized full-res tiles (2760Ã—1504 shown at â‰¤460 px) toward their display size.\n3. That work targets the remaining ~500 MB tracked payload; the preload fix in this task already eliminates the ~150 MB preload / ~410 MB decode waste independently.\n\n## Files changed\n- `game.js` â€” `preloadTileImages()` retargeted to `_hex.png` + deduped (with explanatory comment).",
